WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.478
Moving content to another Orchard Core site can start on the content items list.

00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:06.420
Three actions there export a content item:

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.089
download it as JSON, add it to a deployment plan, or send it

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:10.262
to a deployment target.

00:00:10.262 --> 00:00:11.920
Let's enable them and try each one.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.227
Three features add actions to the Actions menu of a content item.

00:00:21.227 --> 00:00:26.067
View Or Download Content As JSON shows the item as a JSON document,

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.990
and saves it as a file.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.732
Add Content To Deployment Plan puts a Content Item step in a plan you choose.

00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:36.800
Each time the plan runs, it exports the item.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.370
Export Content To Deployment Target sends the items you select once, through a

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.379
target such as File Download.

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:47.650
It uses one plan, which you choose in the settings.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.119
The actions appear for users with the Export Data permission.

00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:55.339
Adding to a plan also needs Manage deployment plans.

00:00:55.339 --> 00:00:57.060
Administrators have both.

00:01:01.274 --> 00:01:05.707
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for content items list.

00:01:05.707 --> 00:01:07.467
Three features match:

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:12.812
View Or Download Content As JSON, Add Content To Deployment Plan, and Export

00:01:12.812 --> 00:01:15.094
Content To Deployment Target.

00:01:15.578 --> 00:01:22.135
Each lists Deployment among its dependencies, and enabling a feature enables its dependencies too.

00:01:22.135 --> 00:01:26.358
Let's select the three, open Bulk Actions, and choose Enable.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:31.654
When the page reloads, each of the three rows shows the Enabled badge.

00:01:31.654 --> 00:01:36.643
The export action also uses a deployment plan, which the settings choose.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:46.996
On the content items list, let's open the Actions menu of Apple Harvest Schedule.

00:01:46.996 --> 00:01:53.754
After a divider, below Unpublish, Delete and Clone, come View as JSON and Download as JSON.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.357
View as JSON opens the item in a text editor, under the title

00:01:58.357 --> 00:02:00.028
View As JSON Article.

00:02:00.028 --> 00:02:04.360
The editor shows the content item with all its parts and fields.

00:02:04.815 --> 00:02:09.607
Download saves the document as a file named after the item's identifier.

00:02:09.607 --> 00:02:11.635
Cancel returns to the list.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:17.888
On the list, Download as JSON saves the same document directly, and the menu closes.

00:02:17.888 --> 00:02:21.748
Both options export the published version of the item.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.667
Let's add Apple Harvest Schedule to a plan.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:32.030
Open its Actions menu and choose Add to Deployment Plan.

00:02:32.495 --> 00:02:37.363
The Available Deployment Plans dialog has a card for every plan on the site.

00:02:37.363 --> 00:02:39.915
Let's select Orchard Harvest Content.

00:02:40.403 --> 00:02:42.853
The list reloads with a notification:

00:02:42.853 --> 00:02:46.043
Content added successfully to the deployment plan.

00:02:46.502 --> 00:02:52.312
Let's open Tools, Deployments, Plans, and choose Manage Steps for Orchard Harvest Content.

00:02:54.686 --> 00:02:58.881
The plan has a Content Item step that shows the title of the article.

00:02:58.881 --> 00:03:03.523
The step stores only the item's identifier, so each run exports the published

00:03:03.523 --> 00:03:05.146
version at that moment.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.034
To add several items, select their checkboxes.

00:03:10.034 --> 00:03:14.761
When two or more are selected, an Actions menu appears above the list.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:17.000
Choose Add to deployment plan.

00:03:17.466 --> 00:03:21.041
A confirmation dialog asks about the bulk action.

00:03:21.041 --> 00:03:25.266
Select Ok, then select the plan in the dialog that follows.

00:03:25.806 --> 00:03:27.864
The same notification appears.

00:03:27.864 --> 00:03:30.722
Let's open the plan again with Manage Steps:

00:03:30.722 --> 00:03:33.866
each selected item has its own Content Item step.

00:03:38.087 --> 00:03:41.411
Enabling the export feature creates a plan for it.

00:03:41.411 --> 00:03:48.117
Let's open Tools, Deployments, Plans, and choose Manage Steps for Export content to deployment plan target.

00:03:48.591 --> 00:03:52.098
Its only step is Export Content To Deployment Target.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:56.081
It stands for the items you select in the content items list.

00:03:56.554 --> 00:03:59.354
Then open Settings, Deployment Targets.

00:03:59.354 --> 00:04:02.963
Deployment Plan lists the plans that have this step.

00:04:02.963 --> 00:04:08.314
Choose it and select Save; without such a plan, the page asks you to create one.

00:04:12.614 --> 00:04:17.128
Once the plan is chosen, the Actions menu offers Export to Deployment Target.

00:04:17.128 --> 00:04:19.794
Let's choose it for Apple Harvest Schedule.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:24.539
The Available Targets dialog lists each target with a description.

00:04:24.539 --> 00:04:30.192
File Download downloads a plan locally, and a configured remote instance appears here too.

00:04:30.192 --> 00:04:33.019
A separate video covers remote deployment.

00:04:33.481 --> 00:04:35.197
Let's select File Download.

00:04:35.197 --> 00:04:39.981
The site runs the plan with this item, and the browser saves a zip deployment package.

00:04:41.632 --> 00:04:48.902
For several items, select two or more checkboxes, open Actions, and choose Export to deployment target.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.151
Confirm with Ok, and select File Download.

00:04:53.151 --> 00:04:55.800
The package holds every selected item.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.635
Download as JSON saves one item, Add to Deployment Plan keeps it in

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:06.808
a plan, and Export to Deployment Target sends items once.

00:05:06.808 --> 00:05:08.530
Thanks for watching.

